 "answer_html": "<h3>Definition</h3><p>Servlet parameters are the values sent by an HTML form (or URL). A servlet reads them with methods of <b>ServletRequest</b>.</p><h3>Key points</h3><ul><li><code>String getParameter(String name)</code>: one value (null if not sent).</li><li><code>String[] getParameterValues(String name)</code>: many values (checkboxes).</li><li><code>Enumeration getParameterNames()</code>: all parameter names.</li><li>Values are Strings; convert with Integer.parseInt().</li></ul><h3>Input page (index.html)</h3><pre>&lt;form action=\"FactorialServlet\" method=\"post\"&gt;\n  Enter Number: &lt;input type=\"number\" name=\"num\" required&gt;\n  &lt;input type=\"submit\" value=\"Calculate Factorial\"&gt;\n&lt;/form&gt;</pre>",
 "quiz": {
  "q": "What does getParameter() return?",
  "options": [
   "int",
   "String",
   "Object[]"
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "why": "Get Param, Parse, Print: parse because it is a String."
 }
